      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs are trimming camp with purpose now, and the edges are starting to show. <strong>They finished the preseason with back-to-back wins over Ottawa - 6-1 and 4-2 - after dropping both split-squad games to Montreal earlier in the week.</strong> That's the sort of messy but useful September ledger that tells a club what it needs to know: the roster is close, not settled. Toronto heads into Tuesday's regular-season opener against Montreal with the mood sharpened by the Arizona stopover and the visit to the Mayich family - a reminder that hockey's hard edge is never far from the human one. The cuts have started, the lines are taking shape, and the veterans are trying to make the young legs fit. <strong>What matters now is who survives the final roster squeeze and who gets the first crack at opening night.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
