      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The last month has shrunk into a tidy, ruthless verdict: baseball in Toronto ends today, and the scoreboard says why. <strong>The Blue Jays dropped 5-1 to the Reds on Saturday</strong>, falling to 78-83 and 5th in the AL East, with a season that has long since slipped into the off-season's cold light. Max Scherzer gets the ball in the finale, and that alone gives the afternoon some bite - one last old-master start, one more chance to watch a future Hall of Famer work before the questions turn to October decisions. The younger hands have been getting their look, and they should keep getting it. <strong>What matters next is simple: Scherzer's swan song, then a winter built around adding starting pitching, tightening the lineup, and deciding which kids can be trusted in 2027</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
