        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The arrival of Kawhi Leonard has changed the temperature in Toronto - now the questions are sharper, the stakes higher, and the margins thinner. <strong>With Kawhi Leonard in tow, Bobby Webster is setting the bar high for the Raptors</strong>, and that is exactly how a franchise should behave in training camp, not drift. The roster is mostly settled, but the real work is in the battles behind the stars: who earns minutes, who backs up Jakob Poeltl, and whether RJ Barrett can fit cleanly into a faster, more coherent plan. Toronto opens preseason Saturday against Miami, with the regular season waiting on Oct. 21 against Chicago. For now, this is a camp built on expectation and pressure - no hiding, no excuses. <strong>Watch the depth chart hard over the next week; that will tell you more than any slogan ever could.</strong>",
