      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The season has already taken on the smell of survival. Washington is 0-2, fourth in the NFC East, and staring up from two games back after <strong>Jayden Daniels' dislocated left elbow sent the offense into Marcus Mariota's hands again</strong>. That is the story now - not promise, not theory, but triage. Daniels will miss today's 1:00 p.m. kickoff against Seattle, and the Commanders are carrying a second straight loss after the 37-20 thumping by Dallas and the 24-22 gut-punch from Philadelphia. Mariota did his work in relief last week, and now he gets the whole show. The margin for error is already paper-thin. <strong>What matters next is whether Washington can keep this from becoming a season defined by one injury and one bad start.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
